cmu-mohawk-gunnery-control-help = First calibrate the grounded M90 hardpoint with a screwdriver, then program your faction IFF with a multitool. Take control while seated and landed or during an active CAS flyby. PGU-410 Squall holds 1200 rounds, deals 20 piercing damage, and fires ten rounds per second (600 RPM). It is the only ground-compatible feed. All ground fire is limited to twenty tiles and a 225-degree forward arc; rounds stop at the cursor. Normal and Night optics cannot see or track through walls; Thermal sees through walls, but rounds still stop on them. Explosive shells heat the barrels faster than Squall; at full heat the M90 locks out until it cools to forty percent. Active CAS flybys support all M90 ammunition: select an active signal flare on the right TARGET monitor for impacts within ten tiles. Airborne shots arrive after three seconds, with a marker during the final second. Explosive shells fire three per second. Mouse aims; hold left click to fire. The turret slews at sixty degrees per second. WASD moves camera and turret. AR shows the firing radius. Mark then Authorize fire for thirty seconds for manual tracking. AI scanning requires activation. Approve each AI target separately. Ground AI requires landing on the planet, a seated gunner with the console open, and renewed approval every thirty seconds. AI cannot acquire or shoot through walls, including in Thermal. Manual control pauses AI; disabling AI starts a five-minute cooldown. Disabling IFF removes friendly shot and impact protection. At zero integrity the M90 requires a staged engineer rebuild.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ground-only = Chin-gun control requires landing or an active CAS flyby; it is unavailable during ordinary transit, takeoff, or tactical hover.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ammo-ground-only = This ammunition cannot be used while airborne. Select an airborne-compatible feed.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ammo-air-only = Explosive M90 ammunition is flyby-only. Select PGU-410 Squall for groundside fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-busy = Another operator is controlling the chin turret.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-range = The target is outside the chin turret's range.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-arc = The target is behind the chin turret's forward firing arc.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-auth-expired = Fire authorization expired. Confirm the target again to resume.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unsafe-shot = Holding fire: a friendly or an opaque obstruction is in the firing path.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-flare-invalid = Flare targeting requires an active CAS flyby and a selected active signal flare. Aim within ten tiles of that flare.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-help = Press this button, then click a visible target in the left camera. Squall can mark living entities; explosive ammunition can mark any entity. Marking never authorizes fire or bypasses friendly safety.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-pending = Click a target in the left camera.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unmarked = No marked target.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire = Acquire priority target
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire-help = Mark the nearest or highest-health visible hostile, according to the priority setting. With a flare selected, acquire only within ten tiles of it. Then authorize fire separately.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize = Authorize fire (30 seconds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize-help = Mark or acquire a target first. Authorizes that entity for thirty seconds, firing only while visible and safe.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-distance = Priority: nearest
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-health = Priority: highest health
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-clear-flare = Clear flare / recenter
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-pan-help = Pan two tiles with the arrows. The center button recenters on the flare or chin mount. Panning clears tracking and authorization.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-short-help = Mouse: aim | Hold click: fire
    Mark -> Authorize: tracked fire
    WASD / arrows: pan | AR: main view
    Airborne TARGET: select a flare
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-flare-only = Airborne M90 fire requires an active CAS flyby and a selected signal flare. Landed fire uses physical Squall rounds.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-preview = CAS flyby: ten tiles around the flare | Impact: 3s, final 1s marked | Squall: 10/s; explosive: 3/s
